  "solution": {
    "text": "The electronic configurations of cations in the given salts are as follows <br/><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></math>  <br/>Hence only <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> ion has one unpaired electron in 3d orbital it means d-d electronic transition is possible, so its salt is coloured."
  }
